	'k02a91690' => '3 visits',
	'k03a0577b' => 'We believe clinical pricing should be transparent, straightforward, and predictable. There are no hidden charges or unexpected add-ons for the treatments provided at Ayumi Podiatry.',
	'k06b8f673' => '“I didn’t need new feet. I needed someone to watch me walk.”',
	'k09dd2175' => 'Daniel&#x27;s Story: Line Cook with Forefoot Burning',
	'k0c92299f' => 'Rather than outsourcing your prescription insoles to an anonymous off-site manufacturing facility, all Ayumi Podiatry orthotics are produced in our Eastgate workshop by orthotics technician Priya Raman. Priya works in direct communication with Lena Marsh and Tomás Ribeiro, reviewing the clinical gait notes and pressure data before shaping each layer of material. Working on site allows us to modify arch profiles, heel cup depth, and forefoot cushioning with meticulous precision. Because our technician is located right down the hall from our consulting rooms, adjustments and fine-tuning can be completed quickly and accurately to meet your specific workplace needs.',
	'k0ce6f6fe' => 'Amara&#x27;s Story: Postal Carrier with Shin Pain',
	'k0f1513c4' => 'Corns, Calluses and Cracked Heels',
	'k0f608e79' => 'Rosa&#x27;s Story: Ward Nurse with Heel Pain',
	'k0f9b6f74' => 'Podiatrist, co-founder',
	'k105078d2' => 'Scroll',
	'k11e9e375' => 'Ten metres, barefoot and in your work shoes.',
	'k13b76140' => 'Shin splints',
	'k14e3176f' => 'Read three stories',
	'k16a112b7' => 'One outcome',
	'k172d5e18' => 'Bunions occur when the joint at the base of your big toe shifts out of alignment, creating a painful bony bump that rubs against footwear. This issue is frequently aggravated by narrow work shoes, steel-toe safety boots, or hours of continuous weight-bearing that force the toes together. The joint often becomes red, stiff, and tender, making walking uncomfortable by the end of the day. Usually treated with: footwear modifications to provide a wider toe box, custom orthotics to relieve mechanical pressure on the first metatarsal head, padding, and joint mobilisation exercises.',
	'k18298940' => 'Step-Free Accessibility and Facilities',
	'k1868eddd' => 'Your First Visit',
	'k19d43b4f' => 'Lena Marsh and Tomás Ribeiro established Ayumi Podiatry in 2015 after noticing how many patients struggled with pain brought on by long working hours on hard floors. Rather than offering temporary fixes, they wanted a practice built entirely around the demands of standing professions. Our clinic hours run from 07:30 to 19:30 on weekdays and 08:00 to 14:00 on Saturdays specifically so healthcare workers, hospitality staff, retail workers, and tradespeople can attend before or after their shifts. We understand that your feet cannot take time off just because they ache, so we provide accessible, attentive clinical care that fits into demanding work schedules.',
	'k1a13e653' => 'Crafted Locally by Priya Raman',
	'k1ad0f27c' => 'Heel pain is the most frequent complaint among workers who stand for extended shifts on concrete or tiled floors. The plantar fascia, a thick band of tissue running under your foot, becomes strained and inflamed under prolonged load, causing sharp stabbing pain during your first steps in the morning or toward the end of a shift. Left untreated, chronic heel irritation can alter how you step and lead to secondary knee or back discomfort. Usually treated with: comprehensive gait assessment, targeted calf and arch loading exercises, custom orthotics to distribute plantar pressure, and supportive footwear advice.',
	'k1af9b667' => 'Gait assessment, sport and work-boot problems and orthotics prescription.',
	'k1fd05cf8' => 'Flat feet',
	'k204adc59' => 'Clinicians and Practice Team',
	'k21900d2e' => 'Work-Boot and Shoe Rubbing',
	'k2240f4e2' => 'Achilles pain',
	'k224553a9' => 'Work-boot rubbing',
	'k229eb040' => 'Conditions',
	'k24841e03' => 'Lena Marsh — Podiatrist and Co-Founder',
	'k268f3d52' => 'On your feet<br>all day?',
	'k26d98a7c' => 'Yes, we offer six dedicated on-site parking spaces directly adjacent to our building at 22 Mercer Yard in Eastgate for our patients. Our ground-floor clinic features a completely step-free entrance, making access easy if you are walking with a limp, using crutches, or using a wheelchair. If you are travelling by public transit, our clinic is well served by local bus and tram lines, with stops situated within a short two-minute walk from our front door. Secure outdoor bicycle racks are also available right outside our entrance for those who cycle.',
	'k279fc767' => 'Diabetes can impair peripheral circulation and nerve sensation in your lower extremities, diminishing your ability to feel cuts, hot spots, or excessive friction. A minor blister from a work shoe can quickly worsen into an unnoticed ulcer if sensation is reduced. Routine preventative screening ensures your feet remain safe, healthy, and protected throughout your working life. Usually treated with: comprehensive annual diabetic foot checks, monofilament sensory testing, vascular pulse assessment, preventative skin care, and protective pressure-relieving footwear guidance.',
	'k27f196a1' => 'We have designed our Eastgate premises to be fully accessible for every visitor, including patients with acute foot pain or mobility impairments. Our entrance is completely step-free with wide automatic glass doors and level flooring throughout the reception area and corridors. Inside each consultation room, our clinical treatment chairs lower smoothly to wheelchair height, allowing comfortable transfers for all patients. If you require assistance upon arrival or have specific accessibility needs, please let Jonas Becker know when scheduling your visit so our team can prepare for your arrival.',
	'k2876b45c' => 'Every successful clinical outcome starts with understanding the unique physical demands of your job. During the first fifteen minutes of your consultation, Lena Marsh or Tomás Ribeiro sits down with you to discuss your daily working routine, the hard surfaces you stand on, the shifts you complete, and the specific history of your pain. We look closely at the wear patterns on your everyday work shoes and talk through any previous treatments you have tried. Listening thoroughly allows us to grasp how your symptoms affect your livelihood so we can design a treatment pathway that fits your reality.',
	'k2a7bb67d' => '15 minutes',
	'k2b8926d6' => 'What a visit feels like',
	'k2cc261a3' => 'Our Clinical Values',
	'k2da4686f' => 'Shin Splints and Achilles Pain',
	'k2f3ccbf7' => 'An ingrown toenail develops when the curved edge of the nail penetrates the surrounding skin, leading to acute pain, swelling, redness, and potential infection. This painful condition is particularly common among workers wearing rigid work boots or heavy protective footwear that compresses the toes together during repetitive walking. Prompt clinical attention relieves discomfort quickly and prevents deeper soft tissue complications. Usually treated with: gentle clinical nail resection, conservative nail edge dressing, foot-care nursing by Grace Mensah, advice on proper nail trimming techniques, and appropriate protective toe spacing.',
	'k301ef5a9' => 'When you arrive at our clinic at 22 Mercer Yard in Eastgate, you will find a calm, unhurried space designed for ease and comfort. We know that attending an appointment around a busy shift can feel stressful, so Jonas Becker greets you promptly at reception and ensures everything runs on time. Inside the private treatment room, your clinician sits with you to discuss your routine before examining your feet. We do not rush you through a generic checklist. Every consultation allows dedicated time to ask questions, examine painful areas gently, and agree on a clear treatment pathway together.',
	'k30b236e9' => 'Treat and adjust',
	'k367906dd' => 'Custom orthotics',
	'k36e1e09f' => 'Book online',
	'k378ca739' => 'Our story',
	'k3a4b731f' => 'Rosa had spent months limping to the bus stop after twelve-hour shifts on the hospital ward. Sharp morning heel pain had gradually turned into an ache that lasted all day, making even short errands exhausting after work.',
	'k3b0e95a7' => 'Our work is guided by three core clinical principles: listen first, explain plainly, and aim for fewer visits rather than more. We begin every appointment by listening carefully to your daily physical demands and personal history. When explaining what is happening with your feet, we avoid confusing medical jargon and give you straightforward answers about your diagnosis and practical options. Most importantly, our treatment plans are designed to resolve your problem efficiently. We want to give you lasting relief, effective home exercises, and proper footwear guidance so you can get back to your work without needing endless follow-up appointments.',
	'k3cbe8173' => '30 min',
	'k3d9c79fd' => 'Ayumi Podiatry was founded in 2015 to provide dedicated foot care for people who spend their working days on their feet. We combine clinical assessment, gait analysis, and practical treatment to keep you working comfortably.',
	'k3dd03346' => 'Your initial appointment is a comprehensive sixty-minute session dedicated entirely to understanding your foot health. For $120, your podiatrist conducts a thorough physical examination, palpates painful structures, evaluates joint range of motion, and observes your gait along our ten-metre walkway both barefoot and in your work shoes. This extended time allows us to identify the underlying mechanical triggers behind your pain rather than rushing through symptoms. We begin initial treatment during this visit and provide you with a written management plan outlining our findings, practical footwear recommendations, and targeted rehabilitation exercises for your shifts.',
	'k3e01e507' => 'Location, Contact and Opening Hours',
	'k3e3214f0' => 'Every foot carries a different day.',
	'k3ea577f5' => 'Mon–Fri 07:30–19:30<br>Sat 08:00–14:00<br>Closed Sun and public holidays',
	'k40444ae2' => 'Podiatry clinic · Eastgate · Since 2015',
	'k40b6c95a' => 'Custom orthotics, one pair (two visits)',
	'k41f87f02' => 'Insurance Receipts and Cancellation Policy',
	'k4737fe14' => 'Clinical Treatments and Services',
	'k47e7c21d' => 'Lena Marsh co-founded Ayumi Podiatry in 2015 to create a clinical space focused on the physical realities of standing workers. With over a decade of clinical experience in biomechanics and general podiatric medicine, Lena leads our care for persistent heel and arch pain, complex nail conditions, and comprehensive diabetic foot management. She believes that unhurried listening and careful clinical observation are the foundations of effective podiatry. Inside the consulting room, Lena takes time to understand how your pain interferes with your livelihood, guiding you through gentle, practical treatment plans that keep you working safely.',
	'k48c7c41b' => 'Step',
	'k48e6697a' => 'Amara walks several miles each day carrying a heavy shoulder satchel along residential delivery routes with varying pavements and stairs. She developed persistent shin splints and aching arch fatigue that threatened her ability to complete her rounds without significant discomfort. During her gait assessment on our walkway, Tomás Ribeiro observed excessive pronation linked to flat feet and tight calf muscles. In her case, Tomás prescribed custom orthotics to support her medial arches and taught her a structured ten-minute calf routine. Following her rehabilitation, Amara returned comfortably to her full postal round.',
	'k4b14a24a' => 'Care now, a written plan within two working days.',
	'k4cb5506e' => 'Find the clinic',
	'k4ff9fed9' => 'Patient Stories',
	'k508f981c' => 'Clinicians',
	'k51344e4e' => 'Foot pain rarely happens in a vacuum, which is why we ask every patient to bring the footwear they wear during their longest shifts. A foot behaves differently when standing barefoot on a clinic floor compared to walking ten miles in heavy safety boots, clogs, or stiff leather shoes. During your appointment, we take time to observe your gait both barefoot and in your work shoes along our ten-metre walkway. Watching the movement of your arches, ankles, and knees under realistic daily loads helps us pinpoint the exact friction points and mechanical stresses causing your discomfort, ensuring our treatment targets real working conditions.',
	'k536519b6' => 'Our Clinical and Technical Specialists',
	'k539f13b5' => 'Do I need a referral to book an appointment?',
	'k54587d0c' => 'Our clinical examinations and treatments are conducted with gentle care and unhurried technique. During your physical evaluation, we test joint mobility and gently palpate muscles and tendons to identify areas of tenderness, always communicating clearly with you before touching sensitive zones. Routine skin debridement and toenail care are performed with precision instruments and are generally completely painless. If an area is inflamed or painful from hours on your feet, we adjust our pressure accordingly. We will explain every step beforehand so you remain fully comfortable and in control throughout your session.',
	'k54902861' => 'Reaching our clinic is convenient whether you travel by car, public transport, or bicycle. We provide six dedicated on-site parking spaces directly beside Mercer Yard exclusively for patient use during appointments. If you travel by public transit, regular municipal bus and tram services stop within two minutes walk of our entrance on Eastgate High Road. For patients who cycle, sturdy outdoor bicycle racks are situated directly outside the building entrance. Clear directional signs guide you from the courtyard directly to our ground-floor glass entrance door.',
	'k5a915b72' => 'Heel Pain and Plantar Fasciitis',
	'k5b84ff9d' => 'Our custom prescription orthotics are individually fabricated in our Eastgate workshop to support your feet through long standing shifts. We tailor every pair to your foot shape, your work footwear, and your daily physical workload.',
	'k5be5af92' => 'Our Clinical Services and Fees',
	'k5c5c215f' => 'Plantar fasciitis',
	'k5caf83b1' => 'What a Visit Feels Like',
	'k5cfdde7c' => 'Numb toes',
	'k5e706a9b' => 'Visit',
	'k63fa12c0' => 'Can I come straight from a night shift?',
	'k65c3eecb' => 'Yes, you are very welcome to attend your appointment straight from a night shift. Many of our patients are ward nurses, emergency responders, logistics personnel, and hospitality workers who come directly from overnight duty. Our morning hours begin early at 07:30 specifically to accommodate your shift patterns before you head home to sleep. If your feet feel tired, swollen, or sore after working all night, that actually provides our clinicians with a realistic, valuable opportunity to observe how your feet and legs respond to fatigue under peak daily load.',
	'k68e05a95' => 'Call us',
	'k69665804' => 'Step 02: Watch You Walk on Our Walkway',
	'k6a16cdf1' => 'Room 2 · our 10-metre walkway',
	'k6b2b5614' => 'Journal',
	'k6b7752ad' => 'Our clinic is situated at 1F, 22 Mercer Yard, Eastgate. To book an appointment or ask about our services, call our reception desk at +00 20 5180 3360 or send an email to hello@ayumipodiatry.example. We open early and stay open late so you can attend before or after work: Monday to Friday from 07:30 to 19:30, and Saturday from 08:00 to 14:00. We are closed on Sundays and public holidays. Jonas Becker manages bookings and will help you find a suitable appointment time that fits around your shifts.',
	'k6b881fe2' => 'Fees and Appointments',
	'k6cbd4331' => 'Nail and skin care',
	'k6cd3ff7b' => 'Daniel works long evening shifts as a line cook in a busy restaurant kitchen, standing stationary on grease-resistant rubber mats for hours at a time. The sustained downward pressure caused severe burning sensations across the balls of his feet and thick, painful calluses under his metatarsal heads. In his case, Grace Mensah provided gentle scalpel debridement to remove the hardened skin and alleviate localized pressure. Tomás Ribeiro then evaluated his footwear and recommended non-slip kitchen shoes with a noticeably wider toe box. Daniel now returns for routine nail and skin care every eight weeks to maintain comfort.',
	'k6ce2880f' => 'Tomás Ribeiro — Podiatrist and Co-Founder',
	'k6d711be6' => '60 min',
	'k6e390b60' => 'The usual complaints',
	'k6ed97afb' => 'The method',
	'k7191754c' => 'Getting to Eastgate and Parking',
	'k72ff3d3d' => 'We do not assess your feet only while you are resting on an examination couch. For twenty minutes, we evaluate your gait along our dedicated ten-metre walkway, observing how your feet, ankles, knees, and hips move together. We evaluate your mechanics both barefoot and while wearing your everyday work boots or occupational shoes. By watching how your arches flex, how your heels strike the floor, and where maximum pressure accumulates with each stride, we uncover the exact mechanical triggers responsible for your discomfort and identify any compensatory movements you may have developed.',
	'k734e92a3' => 'Call or book',
	'k735207c9' => 'How Your Custom Insoles Are Made',
	'k73fb0a4f' => 'Visit the Clinic',
	'k76a3f49a' => 'Thickened areas of dead skin and deep corns form where sustained friction and high downward pressure concentrate under your soles, heels, or across the balls of your feet. When the skin around the heel margin dries out under heavy daily loads, deep and painful cracks can split open, making standing excruciating. Regular clinical maintenance removes this build-up safely and restores skin flexibility. Usually treated with: painless scalpel debridement, professional emollient therapy, pressure redistribution insoles, and advice on daily moisturising routines for dry skin.',
	'k76d301a1' => 'Watch you walk',
	'k7991d9f4' => 'Ayumi Podiatry is located at 22 Mercer Yard in Eastgate, offering early morning and evening appointments designed around your shift schedule. Here is how to find us, get in touch, and access our clinic.',
	'k7a1c9e20' => 'We offer six clearly defined podiatry services with transparent pricing. First visit and gait assessment takes 60 minutes for $120, providing a complete history, movement analysis, and initial treatment plan. Follow-up treatment takes 30 minutes for $70 for ongoing rehabilitation or manual therapy. Nail and skin care takes 30 minutes for $60 with Grace Mensah. Diabetic foot check takes 30 minutes for $55, covering comprehensive vascular and neurological screening. Custom orthotics cost $380 for one pair across 2 visits, including digital scanning, in-house fabrication, and fitting. Orthotic review and adjustment takes 20 minutes for $40. Payment is accepted by card or cash, itemised receipts are provided for your insurer, and we ask for 24 hours notice to cancel.',
	'k7c241b3a' => 'Diabetic foot check',
	'k7e57b4fb' => 'Standing for hours on hard surfaces places repetitive stress on your feet, ankles, and lower legs. We diagnose and treat the common occupational foot conditions that affect people who work on their feet.',
	'k874f931a' => 'In addition to our co-founders, our clinic relies on skilled technical and nursing specialists. Priya Raman serves as our orthotics technician, running our on-site insole workshop where she handcrafts and adjusts custom prescription orthotics using precise 3D scans and durable materials. Grace Mensah is our foot-care nurse, delivering gentle nail and skin care, callus debridement, and thorough preventative diabetic foot checks for patients needing routine maintenance. Together, Priya and Grace ensure our clinical prescriptions and hands-on maintenance care are delivered to the highest standards of safety, precision, and patient comfort.',
	'k879d32b0' => 'A complete pair of custom prescription orthotics costs $380, which covers your 3D digital foot scan, precision fabrication in our workshop, and your initial twenty-minute fitting session. We design your orthotics to swap easily between your work boots, occupational footwear, and everyday shoes. To maintain your insoles, simply wipe them clean with a damp cloth and mild soap, allowing them to dry naturally away from direct heat sources. With full-time daily wear on hard commercial floors, materials naturally experience gradual compressive fatigue, so we advise having your insoles reviewed and replaced every 12 to 18 months to ensure ongoing structural support.',
	'k89814742' => 'Will the examination or treatment hurt?',
	'k8a2a6d69' => 'Flat Feet and Arch Pain',
	'k8a706f70' => 'Mon–Fri 07:30–19:30 · Sat 08:00–14:00',
	'k8e3b72b3' => 'You do not need to prepare or buy special footwear before you come in. Bring the shoes and boots you actually wear to work, unpolished and worn down as they are. That wear pattern tells us what your feet have been dealing with long before we ask you to take them off.',
	'k8ec7aa82' => 'Cracked heels',
	'k8f57ebee' => 'Notes for people who work standing.',
	'k8f7f4c1c' => 'About',
	'k911ff255' => 'We treat foot and lower-limb pain using a three-stage clinical method: we listen to your story, watch how you walk in your work footwear, and provide targeted care. Below are our clinical method and our full schedule of treatments.',
	'k91e2dbeb' => '20 minutes + review',
	'k931be919' => 'Lena Marsh',
	'k9715de13' => 'No, you do not need a doctor&#x27;s referral to book an appointment at Ayumi Podiatry. As independent primary foot-care clinicians, Lena Marsh and Tomás Ribeiro can examine, diagnose, and treat your foot and lower-limb conditions directly. You can simply schedule an appointment through our online booking system or call Jonas Becker at our Eastgate reception desk. If you have relevant diagnostic letters, previous imaging reports, or medical notes from your doctor or occupational health department, you are welcome to bring them along, but a formal referral letter is never required to receive care.',
	'k97cb43f9' => 'We sit down together.',
	'k9811ed97' => 'Tomás Ribeiro',
	'k9906c684' => 'Your first visit',
	'k9db0533b' => '1F, 22 Mercer Yard, Eastgate',
	'k9e2637d1' => 'Bunions',
	'k9e3decaf' => 'Every person who visits our clinic brings a different working routine and a different pair of feet. Here are three individual stories of working people who found relief, shared using first names only and published with permission.',
	'k9edeb2af' => 'First visit and gait assessment',
	'k9ef76ea2' => 'At Ayumi Podiatry, we see young patients from age 12 and older. Adolescents frequently develop foot, arch, and heel discomfort as their growth plates develop or when participating in intense school sports and part-time jobs. Our clinicians assess adolescent gait patterns, footwear fit, and growth-related heel conditions with the same careful attention we apply to adult occupational injuries. For children younger than 12 years of age, we recommend consulting a specialist paediatric podiatrist who possesses specialised paediatric clinic facilities tailored specifically for early childhood motor development.',
	'ka3701179' => 'We sit down to discuss your shifts, your workplace flooring, your shoes and exactly where you feel discomfort. There is no checklist to rush through: this is the conversation that decides what happens next.',
	'ka5c01b27' => 'Effective podiatry begins with understanding the physical demands of your working day. We avoid generic exercises and temporary fixes. Instead we look for the mechanical cause of the ache, then adjust your gait and your footwear around it.',
	'ka7d4925b' => 'Custom Orthotics',
	'kaa5c3d8f' => '60 minutes · $120',
	'kaa9dbb56' => 'Two podiatrists. One long conversation.',
	'kacaed3d4' => 'You walk along our 10-metre clinic walkway barefoot and in your work shoes while we observe how pressure moves through your soles, how your ankles roll and where your stride shortens.',
	'kae5fff3b' => 'Diabetic and Numb Feet',
	'kaeb41de5' => 'Heels after a long shift. Toes in safety boots. Shins after the stairs.',
	'kb1e038ab' => 'Our team brings together experienced podiatrists, an orthotics technician, a foot-care nurse, and dedicated reception and administrative staff. We work together under one roof to provide calm, consistent care for people who work on their feet.',
	'kb4e7ad6b' => 'Practice manager Ana Kovač oversees all administrative and billing procedures at Ayumi Podiatry. Following your appointment, Ana issues an itemised receipt containing all necessary clinical codes, clinician registration details, and itemised service breakdowns required by private health insurers and workplace health schemes. While coverage depends on your specific insurance policy, our paperwork is formatted to make claiming straightforward and fast. If you need to change your scheduled appointment, we kindly ask that you provide at least 24 hours notice. Advance notice allows Jonas Becker to offer that appointment slot to another worker waiting for urgent pain relief.',
	'kb57cc95f' => 'At Ayumi Podiatry, a gait assessment showed how her arches collapsed under the strain of standing on hard hospital floors. Over three visits, we provided targeted heel care and fitted custom orthotics crafted in our workshop. By her week-six review, she was walking home from late shifts without pain.',
	'kb65a7052' => 'Step 03: Treat, Prescribe and Adjust',
	'kb69693d4' => 'Listen, watch you walk, then treat.',
	'kb6ca296f' => 'Ingrown toenails',
	'kba3b8cb6' => 'For patients',
	'kbcb3b8c0' => 'Diabetic foot checks',
	'kbcb82b85' => 'Conditions We Treat',
	'kbd0bcf0a' => 'Is parking available at the clinic?',
	'kbd6929f5' => 'Listening first',
	'kbdb29139' => 'Ayumi Podiatry is an Eastgate clinic founded in 2015 for people who spend their working shifts standing, walking and carrying. We take the time to examine how you walk, how your work shoes wear and why your feet ache. Early and late hours mean care fits around your shifts.',
	'kbe4db089' => 'Lena Marsh and Tomás Ribeiro founded Ayumi Podiatry in 2015 to give people who work on their feet thorough, unhurried care. Appointments are long enough for you to explain your shifts, show how you walk and ask your questions.',
	'kc0dae569' => 'Bunions and Toe Joint Pain',
	'kc1e30297' => 'Fallen arches or flexible flat feet can cause aching fatigue along the inside of your foot and lower leg, especially during long standing shifts. When the arch collapses under repetitive body weight, the tendons and ligaments work significantly harder to keep you upright and mobile, resulting in persistent dull aches. Supporting the structural alignment of the midfoot relieves strain across the entire leg. Usually treated with: dynamic walkway assessment, custom supportive orthotics tailored to your arch profile, strengthening exercises for intrinsic foot muscles, and structured work-shoe recommendations.',
	'kc5c8c8be' => 'Why We Watch You Walk in Your Work Shoes',
	'kc73d1602' => 'Step 01: Listen to Your Daily Routine',
	'kc826665d' => 'To ensure we obtain an accurate picture of your daily foot function, please bring several items to your appointment. Most importantly, bring the work shoes, safety boots, or service clogs that you wear during your longest shifts, as their wear patterns tell us a great deal about your gait. Please also bring the socks you normally wear on shift, as cushioning and fabric thickness influence shoe fit. If you take regular medications, bring an updated list for our clinical records. Finally, bring any old insoles, off-the-shelf arch supports, or medical orthotics you have used previously.',
	'kc8574b60' => 'First visit &amp; gait assessment<br>60 min · $120',
	'kc94620c9' => 'Rosa&#x27;s twelve-hour shifts, without the limp home.',
	'kc9cb848d' => 'Tomás Ribeiro is co-founder of Ayumi Podiatry and leads our gait assessment and biomechanics service. His clinical focus centres on walking mechanics, sports injuries, safety footwear problems, and precision orthotic prescription. Tomás works extensively with tradespeople, warehouse staff, and runners whose joints and tendons endure heavy daily impacts on concrete floors. Along our ten-metre walkway, he analyses subtle movements in foot posture and ankle stability to uncover mechanical inefficiencies. Tomás designs practical rehabilitative exercise routines and works closely with our workshop to prescribe orthotics that match the exact demands of your boots.',
	'kcb1a708a' => '20 min',
	'kcbb37401' => 'Stories',
	'kcc7a8cb6' => 'Repetitive loading on hard floors and sudden increases in shift walking distance often irritate the Achilles tendon and the muscles along the front and inside of the lower leg. Shin splints and Achilles tendinopathy produce burning aches, morning stiffness, and tightness that worsens with continuous walking or climbing stairs at work. Addressing the mechanical root cause prevents chronic tissue degeneration. Usually treated with: video gait analysis, progressive tendon loading protocols, temporary heel raises, custom functional orthotics, and scheduled recovery strategies.',
	'kce6802b4' => 'Listen',
	'kce761366' => 'Heel pain',
	'kcef69d33' => 'Your sixty-minute initial appointment follows a structured five-part clinical flow. First, you book online or by phone with Jonas Becker. Second, you spend fifteen minutes talking with your clinician about your work shifts, your occupational footwear, and exactly where it hurts. Third, you spend twenty minutes walking along our ten-metre walkway, assessed both barefoot and in your work shoes. Fourth, we dedicate twenty minutes to hands-on initial treatment or developing a detailed written plan. Fifth, we follow up by emailing your complete management plan within two working days and scheduling a review in four to six weeks to monitor progress.',
	'kcf69725c' => 'Ingrown Toenails',
	'kd0c65670' => 'We dedicate a full sixty minutes to your initial consultation so we can thoroughly evaluate your foot pain and understand your work routine. Here is what to expect during your appointment and how to prepare.',
	'kd1385016' => 'Our Front Desk and Practice Administration',
	'kd3a280d3' => 'We begin hands-on care straight away, prescribe custom orthotics if they are needed, and email a written plan within two working days. A review follows in four to six weeks, so the plan can change with you.',
	'kd6c7c979' => 'The final part of your consultation focuses on immediate hands-on treatment and clear forward planning. Depending on your clinical diagnosis, your clinician may provide hands-on joint mobilisation, precision nail or callus treatment, custom strapping, or 3D digital scanning for custom orthotics. We also supply a tailored plan with targeted exercises and clear footwear modifications. If orthotics are prescribed, your treatment includes a dedicated fitting visit and a follow-up review to make fine adjustments, ensuring your insoles support your feet comfortably through the demands of your longest shifts.',
	'kd6d73c8b' => 'Your first appointment lasts 60 minutes and includes a full discussion of your shifts and shoes, a walking analysis on our 10-metre track, and an immediate treatment or a clear written plan. Cards and cash are both fine, and you will get an itemised receipt for your insurer.',
	'kd7136a63' => 'Your First Visit for $120',
	'kd93bc589' => 'What to Bring to the Clinic',
	'kdad1fa80' => 'Follow-up treatment',
	'kdca8ed72' => 'Treatments',
	'kdf3e6965' => 'Custom orthotics at Ayumi Podiatry are made in four straightforward stages. First, during your consultation, your clinician performs a detailed gait assessment and takes an accurate 3D scan of your feet under semi-weight-bearing conditions. Second, Priya Raman crafts your bespoke insoles in our on-site workshop over seven working days, selecting durable medical-grade materials suited to your body weight and work environment. Third, you return for a twenty-minute fitting appointment where we test the insoles inside your work shoes and make immediate adjustments. Fourth, you attend a review appointment at week six for $40 to assess your comfort and fine-tune the contouring.',
	'kdf8b36f9' => 'Do you see children at the clinic?',
	'kdf94204b' => 'About Ayumi Podiatry',
	'ke073deae' => 'How your insoles are made',
	'ke4c28905' => 'Pain at the end of a shift is never just about bone or tendon. It is about twelve hours on hard hospital vinyl, a kitchen floor that never softens, or six miles of pavement carrying mail in all weather. We start every first appointment by listening to your routine, your shoes, and exactly when the ache begins.',
	'ke79c6603' => 'Meet the team',
	'ke87e9581' => 'Founded in 2015 for Working People',
	'ke963b2a4' => 'See the conditions we treat',
	'ke9e7cc66' => 'Mon–Fri 07:30–19:30<br>Sat 08:00–14:00',
	'kec6e90f3' => 'The Five Stages of Your First Consultation',
	'kec7d4e3a' => 'Heel and arch pain care, nail conditions and diabetic foot checks.',
	'kecddd364' => 'Our administrative team ensures your visit to Ayumi Podiatry is calm, organized, and unhurried from your very first phone call. Jonas Becker manages reception and patient bookings, scheduling early morning or evening appointments around your shift patterns and answering initial queries with warmth and efficiency. Ana Kovač is our practice manager, overseeing clinic operations, handling billing inquiries, and preparing detailed itemised receipts formatted for health insurance reimbursement. Jonas and Ana make sure you are welcomed promptly, seen on schedule, and supported with clear paperwork after your consultation.',
	'ked37d44b' => 'Corns &amp; calluses',
	'ked6722d3' => 'Review at week 6',
	'kf1d4d130' => 'Safety footwear, steel-toe boots, and standard non-slip service shoes are essential for physical safety, but their rigid materials frequently cause blistering, bruised toenails, and severe pressure points. Friction and moisture trapped inside heavy boots during long shifts break down the outer skin layers and produce persistent soreness. Finding the right balance of protection and anatomical fit is essential. Usually treated with: tailored in-shoe pressure relief, boot fitting guidance, moisture-wicking sock recommendations, orthotic offloading, and specialised protective toe padding.',
	'kf2a4fc6f' => 'Pricing and Wear Guidelines',
	'kf2c9e3fb' => 'Most foot pain builds quietly over weeks and months of standing. Whether it is a sharp morning stab in the heel, burning forefoot calluses from kitchen tiles, or aching shins from postal rounds, these are not signs you have to endure. We assess the mechanics behind the strain and put together a clear, manageable plan to relieve it.',
	'kf31f3ebb' => '20 minutes',
	'kf35a6825' => 'Orthotic review and adjustment',
	'kfa034b35' => 'Appointments run early and late so care fits around your shifts.',
	'kfb10ec17' => 'Rosa works twelve-hour hospital ward shifts on hard vinyl flooring, spending almost all of her working hours moving between patients. Over several months, she developed severe heel pain that felt like a sharp bruise with every step, leaving her limping to the bus stop after late shifts. In her case, Lena Marsh identified plantar fasciitis aggravated by repetitive heel striking in unsupportive clogs. Over three visits, Lena prescribed custom orthotics made in our workshop, introduced calf stretches, and conducted an orthotic review at week six. In her case, Rosa now walks home after her shifts without limping.',
	'kfc206df9' => 'First visit',
	'kfca8a5d7' => 'Book a first visit',
	'search_results' => 'Search results for: %s',
);
